# ⚠️ STALE — DO NOT REBUILD FROM THIS FILE (note updated 2026-10-27)
# This copy is older than the live VM's root crontab and is NOT what runs.
# What is known to differ (from the 2026-09-22 Cloud Shell reading, the
# 2026-09-25 clock fix and the runs' own published config - see WIKI.md
# "The scheduled jobs"); the exact live text is not in the repo:
#   * the trading run is pinned to UTC: a CRON_TZ=UTC bracket holding
#     "35 23 * * *" (cd /root/multi-product-signals, git fetch origin main,
#     then ib_bot.py), so it fires at 23:35 UTC all year - not "35 0" below;
#   * the catch-up lines "0 10" and "0 12" (London) run /root/monday_catchup.sh
#     EVERY day, not Mondays only; 10:00 London = 09:00 UTC in summer and
#     10:00 UTC in winter; the 12:00 line is a retry that exits when the 10:00
#     run succeeded (marker /root/ran_<date>);
#   * every ib_bot.py run talks to IBKR over the Web API (IB_BACKEND=web, OAuth),
#     not through IB Gateway on port 4001;
#   * HK_ENABLED=1 is on the 23:35 line but was NOT in the catch-up run's
#     environment on 2026-10-27 (its published config showed hk_enabled false),
#     so that run places no new HK buys; the owner is adding it there;
#   * also live and not listed here: the hourly ":25" deploy + publish_web.py
#     line (the only one that pulls code), the 10-minute ib_commands.py
#     poller, the "40 23" (London) daily_signal.py digest and the 2-minute
#     telegram_poll.py. Whether the Gateway-era lines below still run is not
#     recorded.
# The owner will paste the live crontab (sudo crontab -l) so this copy can be
# refreshed. Until then, dump the real one before any edit or rebuild.
#
# Older note (2026-08-01), kept for the record:
# The live VM differs: it also runs an hourly :20 publish, a ~10-min
# ib_commands.py poller, and an additional weekday trading run at 09:00 UTC
# that is not listed here. Timings below also disagree with observed runs
# (daily trading fires 23:35 UTC, not 00:35). Dump the real one before any
# edit or rebuild:  ssh ... 'sudo crontab -l'
# setup_vm.sh is likewise stale: it installs a PAPER gateway (port 4002) and
# a --dry crontab line, and copies none of the vm_ops/*.sh scripts.
# Root crontab on the multi-product-bot VM (reference copy, v2 2026-07-20)
# UTC section
35 0 * * * cd /root/multi-product-signals/execution && IB_PORT=4001 CONFIRM_FIRST=0 python3.11 ib_bot.py >> /root/bot.log 2>&1 && touch /root/ran_$(date -u +\%F)
*/15 * * * * /root/ensure_gateway.sh
# UK-time section (handles BST/GMT automatically).
# IBKR's weekly 2FA demand is anchored ~Mon 01:00 UK (Sun 20:00 ET week-start);
# user ignores the 1am push, approves the Mon 07:30 one; catch-up trades at 10:00.
CRON_TZ=Europe/London
30 7 * * 1 /root/weekly_reauth.sh
30 8 * * 1 /root/reauth_check.sh
30 9 * * 1 /root/reauth_check.sh
0 11 * * 1 /root/reauth_check.sh
0 9 * * * /root/reauth_check.sh
0 10 * * 1 /root/monday_catchup.sh
0 12 * * 1 /root/monday_catchup.sh
